<p>Actually, cloning the scene is needed for transactional load (parse into=
 temp, then replace). I'll implement scene_clone or just parse into a fresh=
 Scene and swap. Since Scene uses pointers, I can parse into a temp Scene a=
nd, on success, free the old and copy pointers. Simpler: parse function tak=
es a Scene* and fills it (caller passes a fresh Scene). For transactional l=
oad, caller allocates temp Scene, parses, validates; on success swaps into =
the live document (free live, move temp). I'll implement scene_move.</p>
<p>Let me write scene.h and scene.c. This is getting large but necessary.</=
p>
