-8; if invalid, PBT_E_UTF8. That matches "invalid UTF-8 in user-facing quot=
ed strings is a parse error" and the malformed/invalid_utf8.pbt exists. The=
 invalid_utf8.pbt is 35 bytes =E2=80=94 let me check it triggers PBT_E_UTF8=
.)</li>
<li>Split into lines (handle LF and CRLF). Line length limit (PBT_E_LINE_TO=
O_LONG) =E2=80=94 the line_too_long.pbt is ~1MB line. Hard limit: I'll set =
a large line limit, say 1 MiB? Actually the malformed file is 1048595 bytes=
