0; --cr-md-list-padding-left: 1.29em;"><p>Now the scene_write.c. Let me wri=
te it carefully. I'll build a dynamic string buffer.</p>
<p>I'll write helper appends. Then serialize.</p>
<p>Let me be thorough with the per-object-type canonical field order.</p>
<p>For DROP_TARGET: start, end, thickness, restitution, friction, min_hit_s=
peed, base_score, cooldown, initially_raised, reset_mode, reset_delay, enab=
led, layer, locked.<br>
For STANDUP_TARGET: start, end, thickness, restitution, friction, min_hit_s=
peed, base_score, cooldown, enabled, layer, locked.<br>
For ROLLOVER: start, end, width, base_score, activation_mode, enabled, laye=
r, locked. (activation_mode serialized as ON_ENTER)<br>
For ONE_WAY_GATE: start, end, thickness, allowed_direction, restitution, fr=
iction, enabled, layer, locked.<br>
For SLINGSHOT: start, end, thickness, restitution, friction, impulse, base_=
score, cooldown, enabled, layer, locked.<br>
For WALL/RAMP: start, end, thickness, restitution, friction, enabled, layer=
, locked. RAMP also visual_style=E2=80=94skip (not stored).<br>
For BUMPER: center, radius, restitution, friction, impulse, base_score, coo=
ldown, enabled, layer, locked.<br>
For FLIPPER: pivot, length, thickness, rest_angle_deg, active_angle_deg, en=
gage_speed_deg_s, return_speed_deg_s, restitution, friction, input, enabled=
, layer, locked.<br>
For SENSOR: rect (tuple4), enabled, debug_visible, layer, locked.<br>
For DRAIN: rect, enabled, layer, locked.<br>
For BALL_SPAWN: position, initial_velocity, enabled, [ball_radius if has_ba=
ll_radius], layer, locked.<br>
For LAUNCHER: position, spawn, direction, min_speed, max_speed, full_charge=
_time, charge_curve, enabled, layer, locked.<br>
For SPINNER: pivot, half_length, thickness, rest_angle_deg, angular_damping=
, inertia, restitution, friction, score_per_tick, tick_angle_deg, enabled, =
layer, locked.<br>
For KICKOUT: center, capture_radius, eject_direction, eject_speed, hold_tim=
e, base_score, enabled, layer, locked.</p>
<p>I need a numeric formatter that round-trips doubles. I'll write fmt_dbl =
that emits a representation. To match "enough significant digits to round-t=
rip to ~1e-12" and avoid fixed 2-decimal, I'll use %.17g for general double=
s but trim? Simpler: use %.17g. That round-trips exactly. Good enough.</p>
<p>For integers (long), just %ld.</p>
<p>For vectors: "(%.17g, %.17g)".<br>
For tuple4: "(%.17g, %.17g, %.17g, %.17g)".</p>
<p>For booleans: "true"/"false".<br>
For enums: use *_name functions.<br>
For reset_mode: 0-&gt;MANUAL_EVENT,1-&gt;AFTER_DELAY,2-&gt;ON_NEW_BALL.<br>
For charge_curve: 0-&gt;LINEAR,1-&gt;EASE.<br>
For flipper input: 0-&gt;LEFT_FLIPPER,1-&gt;RIGHT_FLIPPER.<br>
For activation_mode (rollover): always ON_ENTER.</p>
<p>For strings: quote with escapes (, ", n, t).</p>
<p>Note: the parser uses PB_NAME_MAX for string max but my parser's parse_s=
tring uses PB_NAME_MAX (256) for name. For writer, scene names are stored i=
n char arrays (PB_NAME_MAX). Fine.</p>
<p>Now the layers: serialize sorted by order. I'll make a temp copy of indi=
ces sorted by order.</p>
<p>Let me write the code. I'll create a growable buffer struct.</p>
<p>One concern: the canonical minimal example includes scene_seed, nudge fi=
elds. For objects, layer + locked required. The writer always emits them. F=
or round-trip, the parser sets layer/locked from file. Good.</p>
<p>Also note: for format 2, the parser requires at least one layer; the wri=
ter emits layers. For v1 scenes migrated to v2 in-memory (format set to 2 b=
y parser with a "gameplay" layer added), the writer will emit that layer. G=
ood.</p>
<p>Let me write scene_write.c.</p>
<p>For atomic save: write to path+".tmp", then rename. On Windows, rename o=
ver existing file should work (replace). I'll use fopen with "wb", fwrite, =
fflush, fclose, then rename. If rename fails, return error. Keep old file i=
ntact (we only rename over it). Good.</p>
