j_count].order =3D s-&gt;obj_count</code>), and s2 also gets order =3D inde=
x on re-parse. So order should be same.</p>
<p>But <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">format</code>: s1.format =3D 2 (migra=
ted from v1). s2.format =3D 2 (parsed v2). Same.</p>
<p><code class=3D"cr-inline-code">has_seed</code>: s1.has_seed =E2=80=94 fo=
r v1 migration, <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">if (!out-&gt;has_seed) out-&=
gt;scene_seed =3D 0;</code> =E2=80=94 has_seed stays 0. For s2 (v2 parse), =
scene_seed is parsed so has_seed=3D1. So has_seed differs (0 vs 1)! And if =
fingerprint hashes has_seed... let me check. The fingerprint I saw hashes l=
ayer.visible/locked as 1 byte, but I didn't see it hash scene.has_seed or s=
