 probably doesn't hash has_seed. Hmm.</p>
<p>Actually, maybe the fingerprint hashes by iterating objects in array ord=
er, and for the migrated v1, the "gameplay" LAYER is added, but its order..=
. The writer re-sorts layers by order. The migration sets gameplay order=3D=
0. In s2, the layer is parsed with order=3D0. Same.</p>
<p>Let me just check the top of scene_fingerprint to see what's hashed (sce=
ne-level). And also I should reconsider: <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">mul=
tiball_stress.pbt</code> ALSO has fp mismatch text_equal=3D1. And <code cla=
ss=3D"cr-inline-code">legacy_editor_full_table_v1</code>. Both are v1 files=
