 actions has a different amount/spawn/count/target/multiplier/duration/drop=
ped between s1 and s2.</p>
<p>Why would actions differ? The event has action_count=3D3. The writer emi=
ts them. On re-parse, they're read back. If the writer doesn't emit some ac=
tion field that fp hashes, OR emits in a way that re-parses to a different =
value...</p>
<p>Actually =E2=80=94 the most likely cause: the event <code class=3D"cr-in=
line-code">event_bonus</code> with trigger=3D0 (TRIG_SENSOR_ENTER) and 3 ac=
tions. The fp hashes each action's amount, spawn, count, target, multiplier=
, duration, dropped. For actions that don't have certain fields set, those =
remain at default (0/empty). On re-parse, if the writer doesn't emit e.g. <=
code class=3D"cr-inline-code">count</code> for an action that had count=3D0=
, the re-parsed action has count=3D0 (default). Equal.</p>
<p>But the value could differ if: an action field in s1 has a non-default v=
alue that the writer doesn't emit, so on re-parse it becomes default. E.g.,=
 if an action has <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">multiplier=3D0</code> but =
fp hashes multiplier... no, 0=3D=3D0.</p>
<p>Hmm. Actually, the issue might be <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">duratio=
n</code>: fp hashes <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">ac-&gt;duration</code> (=
