<p>So duration is used by SET_MULTIPLIER_OVERRIDE, OPEN_GATE, LIGHT_INDICAT=
OR. My writer handles SET_MULTIPLIER_OVERRIDE (emits duration if nonzero) a=
nd OPEN_GATE/LIGHT_INDICATOR (doesn't emit duration).</p>
<p>So I need to emit duration for OPEN_GATE and LIGHT_INDICATOR too. Let me=
 update the writer to emit <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">duration</code> f=
or those action types.</p>
<p>Also, the round-trip requirement says save must preserve all authored pr=
operties. So emitting duration for these is correct.</p>
<p>But note: for SET_MULTIPLIER_OVERRIDE, I only emit duration if nonzero (=
<code class=3D"cr-inline-code">if(ac-&gt;duration)</code>). That's fine sin=
ce 0 is default. But for LIGHT_INDICATOR/OPEN_GATE, duration might legitima=
tely be 0 (no duration). The parser default is 0. So emitting only when non=
zero is fine. But to be safe and match "preserve authored properties", I sh=
ould emit duration for these types when nonzero. Actually the same <code cl=
ass=3D"cr-inline-code">if(ac-&gt;duration)</code> guard works. Let me updat=
e the writer: for OPEN_GATE and LIGHT_INDICATOR, emit duration if nonzero.<=
/p>
<p>Actually, simpler: in the combined case for ENABLE/DISABLE/OPEN_GATE/LIG=
HT_INDICATOR/RESET_TARGET/EJECT_KICKOUT, after emitting target, also emit d=
uration if nonzero. But ENABLE_OBJECT/DISABLE_OBJECT/RESET_TARGET/EJECT_KIC=
KOUT don't have duration semantics. Emitting duration=3D0 wouldn't happen (=
guard). But guard <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">if(ac-&gt;duration)</code>=
 means we only emit when nonzero, so it's safe to add to the shared case. B=
ut RESET_TARGET/EJECT_KICKOUT/ENABLE/DISABLE don't parse duration into a me=
aningful place... Actually the parser DOES parse <code class=3D"cr-inline-c=
ode">duration</code> param for ANY action (the while loop over params handl=
es <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">duration</code>). So if a RESET_TARGET ha=
d <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">duration=3D2.0</code> in the file, the par=
ser would store it. But that's not a valid field for RESET_TARGET per spec;=
 but the parser is lenient. For round-trip, if the file has it, we should p=
reserve it. Emitting it back is fine. But it's cleaner to only emit duratio=
n for the types that semantically use it.</p>
<p>Let me just add <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">if(ac-&gt;duration) buf_p=
rintf(&amp;b," duration=3D%.6g", ac-&gt;duration);</code> to the OPEN_GATE =
and LIGHT_INDICATOR handling. I'll split them out.</p>
