0; --cr-md-block-margin: 8px 0; --cr-md-hr-margin: 12px 0; --cr-md-list-pad=
ding-left: 1.29em;"><p>Now the big one: sim.c. Let me implement the determi=
nistic physics engine. I'll be thorough but focused on the core mechanics.<=
/p>
<p>Key constants (doc 15.1):</p>
<ul>
<li>dt =3D 1/240</li>
<li>epsilon =3D 1e-9</li>
<li>penetration slop =3D 0.02</li>
<li>penetration correction fraction =3D 0.60</li>
<li>discrete contact solver iterations =3D 8</li>
<li>max impact/TOI resolutions per ball per step =3D 16</li>
<li>max event actions per fixed step =3D 4096</li>
</ul>
<p>Let me implement:</p>
<p>sim_init: set pointer, zero.<br>
sim_reset: full reset to fresh session. Spawn initial ball(s) at the first =
BALL_SPAWN. Actually, the game starts with turns_remaining =3D starting_tur=
ns, and spawns balls. For headless determinism, I'll spawn one ball at star=
t (or per max_active_balls). Let me spawn the first enabled BALL_SPAWN ball=
 at reset, set turns_remaining =3D starting_turns, score=3D0.</p>
<p>sim_spawn_ball: create a Ball at spawn object's position with initial_ve=
locity, radius=3Dspawn.ball_radius or default_ball_radius, mass=3Ddefault_b=
all_mass, restitution/friction=3Ddefault. Add to balls[].</p>
<p>sim_step:</p>
<ol>
<li>input phase: sample nudge edges (handled in sim_input, applied here? Ac=
tually doc 15.38 says nudge edges sampled in input phase before kinematic m=
otor update and free-ball acceleration). I'll apply flipper engage states, =
then nudge velocity deltas.</li>
</ol>
<p>Let me structure sim_step:</p>
<ul>
<li>if game_over, return.</li>
<li>step++.</li>
<li>Update mechanism kinematics: flippers move toward target angle by engag=
e/return speed; spinners apply damping.</li>
<li>Apply nudge: for each nudge edge this step, add nudge_impulse to each f=
ree ball velocity (scaled? doc says "add the document-21 velocity delta"). =
The nudge impulse is a velocity delta. Add nudge_impulse * direction to eac=
h free active ball. Then clamp each ball to max speed. Update tilt meter; i=
f reaches threshold, set tilted.</li>
<li>For each active, non-captured, non-drained ball:
<ul>
<li>apply gravity: v +=3D g*dt</li>
<li>apply damping: v <em>=3D exp(-d</em>dt)</li>
<li>speed clamp: if |v|&gt;vmax, scale.</li>
<li>Integrate with CCD against static geometry (capsules, bumpers, flippers=
, spinners, one-way gates, targets, sensors, drains, kickouts). Use sub-ste=
pping via TOI.</li>
<li>ball-ball collisions (after integration, resolve pairwise).</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Resolve events: when triggers fire (bumper hit, sensor enter/exit, drai=
n, target hit, etc.), find matching events and execute actions.</li>
<li>Handle captured balls: decrement timer; eject when expired.</li>
<li>Handle drained balls: remove them (set active=3D0). If ball_count drops=
 to 0, decrement turns_remaining, spawn new ball if turns remain.</li>
<li>Update override multiplier timer.</li>
<li>Check non-finite -&gt; error.</li>
</ul>
<p>This is a lot. Let me implement a reasonable, deterministic version. I'l=
l do CCD for ball vs static capsule and ball vs circle via analytic swept t=
ests. For simplicity and determinism, I'll implement:</p>
<ul>
<li>For each ball, compute the time-of-impact (TOI) against all static coll=
iders within the step, sort by TOI, advance to each TOI, apply collision re=
sponse, continue. Up to 16 impacts.</li>
<li>Then ball-ball: a few iterations of pairwise resolution.</li>
</ul>
<p>Let me implement collision primitives:</p>
<ul>
<li>swept_circle_segment: given ball pos p, vel v, radius r, segment a-b ex=
panded by r (so effectively ball center vs segment with radius R+r). Find e=
arliest t in [0,1] (fraction of dt) where moving point p+t*v touches segmen=
t. Solve quadratic. Returns t and contact normal.</li>
<li>swept_circle_circle: ball vs static circle center c radius Rc. Expand: =
ball center vs circle radius Rc+r. Solve quadratic for earliest t in [0,1];=
 normal =3D (p+hit - c) normalized.</li>
</ul>
<p>For TOI ordering with multiple colliders, I'll collect candidate impacts=
, sort, process.</p>
<p>Given the complexity, let me implement a robust but not overly elaborate=
 CCD. For thin walls (high speed thin wall test), the swept test ensures no=
 tunneling.</p>
<p>Let me write sim.c. It's long. I'll be careful.</p>
<p>Let me define helper: resolve static collision for a ball with a capsule=
 (expanded radius rcap =3D thickness/2): normal impulse + friction + positi=
onal correction.</p>
<p>For flippers: treat as moving capsule. The contact point's surface veloc=
ity =3D omega x r. I'll compute effective relative velocity and apply impul=
se using the ball-surface relative velocity (doc 15.7-8 with v_surface). Fo=
r simplicity, I'll compute v_surface at contact =3D (-omega<em>ry, omega</e=
m>rx) and use that as the static surface velocity in the normal/tangential =
impulse formulas. Good enough and deterministic.</p>
<p>For spinner: similar but with the rigid-body formula (doc 15.33). I'll i=
mplement the spinner normal impulse with K_n =3D 1/m + (an*an)/I.</p>
<p>For bumper: on impact, normal material collision + extra impulse J_bumpe=
r*n + clamp + score + cooldown.</p>
<p>For slingshot: capsule collision + extra outward impulse + score.</p>
<p>For sensor/drain: swept AABB (expanded by ball radius). Sensor: enter/ex=
it events. Drain: drain event.</p>
<p>For kickout: capture on swept center crossing capture circle; eject afte=
r hold_time.</p>
<p>For targets (drop/standup): capsule collision, qualified hit if closing =
normal speed &gt;=3D min_hit_speed; score; drop target becomes non-solid.</=
p>
<p>For rollover: capsule trigger (non-solid), score on crossing.</p>
<p>OK let me write it. This is big but let me do it.</p>
<p>I need to map objects to mechanism runtime arrays. I'll index flippers/s=
pinners/kickouts by their object index in scene-&gt;objects (0..obj_count-1=
), clamped to PB_MAX_RT_OBJ.</p>
<p>Let me also handle events: I'll have a function fire_events_for_trigger(=
sim, obj_id, trigger_type) that finds events with matching source and trigg=
er, executes actions in order. Actions: ADD_SCORE (score +=3D amount * mult=
iplier?), SPAWN_BALL, ENABLE/DISABLE_OBJECT, START_MULTIBALL, SET_MULTIPLIE=
R_OVERRIDE, OPEN_GATE, LIGHT_INDICATOR, RESET_TARGET, SET_TARGET_DROPPED, E=
JECT_KICKOUT, CLEAR_TILT.</p>
<p>The score multiplier: combo_multiplier and override_multiplier. ADD_SCOR=
E amount applies with multiplier =3D override_multiplier? let me apply: eff=
ective =3D amount * max(1, combo_multiplier) * (override_multiplier? overri=
de_multiplier : 1). I'll keep it simple: multiplier =3D override_multiplier=
&gt;0 ? override_multiplier : combo_multiplier&gt;0 ? combo_multiplier : 1.=
 Actually combos aren't fully specified; I'll use override_multiplier if se=
t else 1. Keep deterministic.</p>
<p>Let me write sim.c now.</p>
<p>Given length, I'll write a solid version. Let me be careful with the TOI=
 loop to avoid infinite loops.</p>
