<p>Now let me create some test fixtures that DO trigger validation errors, =
to verify the validation actually catches issues (otherwise it's untested).=
 I'll create deliberately broken valid scenes and confirm scenecheck report=
s the right errors. But that's part of the test suite later. For now, valid=
ation is implemented.</p>
<p>Now let me move to replay. I need:</p>
<ol>
<li>Replay recording from sim (capture input edges at exact steps).</li>
<li>Replay file writing (PINBALL_REPLAY 1 format) =E2=80=94 for the test su=
ite to generate replays.</li>
<li>Replay validation/playback =E2=80=94 already partially in simcheck.</li=
>
<li>replaycheck.exe =E2=80=94 dedicated validator.</li>
<li>detcompare.exe =E2=80=94 first-divergence comparator.</li>
</ol>
<p>Actually, simcheck already supports <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">--rep=
lay</code>. I should add replay <em>recording</em> capability so I can gene=
rate a replay from a play session and verify replay determinism (record, th=
en replay, expect identical final state).</p>
<p>Let me think about how to record. The sim doesn't currently track input =
edges. I'll add a small recorder to simcheck or a separate module. Actually=
, to keep it simple and faithful: replay records logical actions at step in=
dices. I can add to Sim an optional "record" mode that appends actions to a=
 buffer. But that complicates Sim. Alternatively, the app layer records inp=
ut edges and writes the .pbr. For headless determinism test of replay, I ca=
n generate a replay programmatically in a test (e.g., a replay with some LA=
UNCH and FLIPPER events), run it twice, and confirm identical results. That=
 validates replay determinism.</p>
<p>Also doc 07.22 mentions v1.0 logical actions include NUDGE_*. Good, my p=
arser handles them.</p>
<p>Let me design replay module <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">replay.h/repl=
ay.c</code> with:</p>
<ul>
<li><code class=3D"cr-inline-code">int replay_write(const char *path, uint6=
