v_count)</code> =E2=80=94 writes a .pbr file.</li>
<li><code class=3D"cr-inline-code">int replay_parse_file(const char *path, =
Replay *out)</code> =E2=80=94 parse (I already have one in simcheck.c; bett=
er to move to replay.c and reuse).</li>
<li><code class=3D"cr-inline-code">int replay_verify(const Scene *sc, const=
 Replay *rp)</code> =E2=80=94 checks scene_hash matches; returns RPL_E_* co=
de.</li>
<li>A recorder struct to capture events during sim.</li>
</ul>
<p>For detcompare: compare two JSON/checkpoint outputs, report first diverg=
ence. I'll implement detcompare.exe that takes two files (e.g., checkpoint =
JSON Lines or headless JSON) and finds first mismatch.</p>
<p>Actually, detcompare per doc 07.24: "first-divergence reporting across c=
heckpoint/trace outputs." So it compares two checkpoint sequences. Let me i=
mplement detcompare.exe that reads two files (one checkpoint per line, JSON=
) and reports the first line/index where they differ (with field-level deta=
il). And returns non-zero on divergence.</p>
<p>For replay determinism, I'll write a test: generate a replay (via a smal=
l generator), run simcheck --replay twice, compare outputs identical. I can=
 do that in the test harness with shell.</p>
<p>Given time, let me implement:</p>
