padding-left: 1.29em;"><p>Now I need to create build_tests.sh and compile. =
But I'm worried about a few things:</p>
<ol>
<li><code class=3D"cr-inline-code">sc.has_seed</code> and <code class=3D"cr=
-inline-code">sc.scene_seed</code> =E2=80=94 Scene has <code class=3D"cr-in=
line-code">int has_seed;</code> and <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">uint64_t=
 scene_seed;</code>. Good.</li>
<li><code class=3D"cr-inline-code">png_write_rgb</code> signature: <code cl=
ass=3D"cr-inline-code">int png_write_rgb(const char *path, int w, int h, co=
nst unsigned char *rgb);</code>. Good.</li>
<li><code class=3D"cr-inline-code">render_scene</code> signature confirmed.=
</li>
<li><code class=3D"cr-inline-code">fb_init/fb_free/fb_distinct_colors</code=
> uses fb-&gt;pix, fb-&gt;w, fb-&gt;h. Need to confirm Framebuffer struct f=
ields. From render.h earlier: <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">typedef struct=
 {...} Framebuffer;</code> =E2=80=94 I need the field names. Let me check r=
ender.h for Framebuffer definition (pix, w, h). I used fb-&gt;pix, fb-&gt;w=
, fb-&gt;h. Let me verify.</li>
</ol>
<p>Also <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">Framebuffer fb; fb_init(&amp;fb,w,h)=
;</code> then render_scene. Need fb.pix allocated by fb_init. Should be fin=
e.</p>
<ol start=3D"5">
<li>
<p><code class=3D"cr-inline-code">g_fn</code> array of 1500=C3=97220 =E2=80=
=94 that's 330KB on stack? No, it's static. Good (static global). Actually =
it's <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">static char g_fails[1500][220];</code> =
=E2=80=94 global, fine.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">system()</code> calls spawn cmd.exe. =
Using <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">&gt;nul 2&gt;&amp;1</code> redirects. =
On Windows that's fine. The path uses D:/... Good.</p>
</li>
<li>
