rements). Wait =E2=80=94 does sim_step increment at start or end? If sim_re=
set sets step=3D0, and the loop does sim_input (step=3D0) then sim_step (no=
w step becomes 1), next iteration sim_input (step=3D1). So recorded step at=
 iteration i =3D i. Good. apply_replay applies event at step i during itera=
tion i. Matches.</p>
<p>But what if sim_step increments step at the START of the function? Then =
after sim_reset (step=3D0), first sim_input sees step=3D0, then sim_step in=
crements to 1 at start, processes... still event recorded at step 0. Same.<=
/p>
<p>So consistent. I'm skeptical there's a real mismatch. Let me just add de=
