ect minimal scene only wrote the header and a "--" line, NOT the object! Th=
at means scene_write didn't write the object. Why?</p>
<p>Look: scene_write.c line 65 writes "PINBALL_TABLE 2\n\n". Then it presum=
ably iterates objects. But the output shows only "PINBALL_TABLE 2" + "--". =
So the object section wasn't written.</p>
<p>Ah =E2=80=94 maybe scene_write writes objects but my minimal scene's obj=
ect has an EMPTY layer string or something that causes it to be skipped, OR=
 scene_write requires the scene to have a name/meta and the object write is=
 conditional. But fixtures write objects fine.</p>
<p>Wait, the <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">write=3D</code> shows "PINBALL_=
TABLE 2\n--" =E2=80=94 the "--" might be from the next part. Actually the f=
ull write would be "PINBALL_TABLE 2\n\n[meta ...]\n\n[object WALL o0]\n..."=
. But we only see header. So scene_write isn't serializing the object.</p>
<p>Possibility: scene_write writes objects but my minimal scene's <code cla=
ss=3D"cr-inline-code">obj_count</code> =E2=80=94 I did <code class=3D"cr-in=
line-code">scene_add_object(&amp;sc,&amp;o)</code>. That should set obj_cou=
nt=3D1. Unless scene_add_object fails because... let me check scene_add_obj=
ect: it likely reallocs and appends. Should work. But maybe scene_add_objec=
t requires the layer to be valid or something. Or maybe it checks <code cla=
ss=3D"cr-inline-code">o.type</code> validity and rejects. Unlikely.</p>
<p>Hold on =E2=80=94 maybe the issue is that <code class=3D"cr-inline-code"=
>make_minimal()</code> sets <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">sc.format</code>=
? No. Let me look at scene_write.c more carefully. The output "PINBALL_TABL=
E 2\n--" =E2=80=94 maybe after the header it writes "[meta]" with name, the=
n "[object ...]" but the object writing function <code class=3D"cr-inline-c=
ode">write_object</code> returns early for some types or when a field is mi=
ssing/non-finite. For my object, e.g., BALL_SPAWN with position set =E2=80=
=94 should be fine. But maybe write_object for these types requires additio=
nal fields that I didn't set (e.g., WALL requires start/end which I set).</=
