=3D"cr-inline-code">sc-&gt;objects</code> which is allocated via the scene'=
s obj_cap=3D0 initially and needs growth =E2=80=94 scene_init sets objects=
=3DNULL, obj_cap=3D0. scene_add_object must handle growth. If it doesn't (e=
.g., expects pre-allocated), obj_count stays 0. But fixtures are parsed wit=
h obj_count&gt;0, so the parser must grow the array. The add function used =
by parser works. So scene_add_object should work too.</p>
<p>Hmm, but in the type roundtrip test, I do <code class=3D"cr-inline-code"=
>Scene sc=3Dmake_minimal(); ... scene_add_object(&amp;sc,&amp;o); char*out=
=3Dscene_write(&amp;sc);</code>. If scene_add_object works, obj_count=3D1.<=
/p>
<p>Let me just check scene_add_object implementation. And scene_write's obj=
ect loop. Let me read scene_write.c.</p>
<p>Actually, the replay events reveal something important: ev[0] step=3D0 k=
ind=3D0 (L_FLIPPER_DOWN), ev[1] step=3D0 kind=3D2 (R_FLIPPER_DOWN), ev[2] s=
tep=3D0 kind=3D4 (LAUNCH_DOWN). So at step 0, ALL three go down (since L=3D=
(0%20&lt;3)=3D1, R=3D(0%30&lt;4)=3D1, La=3D(0%50&lt;2)=3D1). Then ev[3] ste=
p=3D20 kind=3D0 (L down again at step 20) =E2=80=94 wait, L went 1 at step0=
..2, then 0 at 3..19, then 1 at 20. So DOWN at step 20 (kind 0). But where'=
s the L UP at step 3? It's missing! The events show: step0 L down, step0 R =
down, step0 launch down, step20 L down, step30 R down, step40 L down...</p>
<p>So the UP events are MISSING. That's the bug! The recorder records DOWN =
but not UP. So in reconstruction, L stays 1 forever after step 0 (never goe=
s up). That's why fp diverges =E2=80=94 the flipper is held down the entire=
 time in replay, causing different physics.</p>
<p>So the recorder only records DOWN edges, not UP edges. That means sim_re=
corder_take records only downs, OR sim_input only records downs. Let me che=
ck sim.c's recording logic. The summary said "=E6=8D=95=E8=8E=B7=E4=B8=8A=
=E5=8D=87=E6=B2=BF" (capture rising edge) =E2=80=94 it only records rising =
edges (DOWN), not falling (UP). That's a product limitation/bug in the reco=
rder: it should record both transitions to faithfully replay.</p>
<p>Given the spec requires replay determinism, the recorder should capture =
both DOWN and UP. The current implementation only captures rising edges. I =
should FIX sim.c to record both edges. That's a legitimate product fix.</p>
<p>Let me look at sim.c sim_input recorder code.</p>
