<p>But scene_free might free internal pointers of the object (like layer st=
ring is inline, fine; but some objects have dynamically allocated members?)=
. Let me check if Obj has pointers. Probably all inline (char arrays, Vec2,=
 etc.). So <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">sc.obj_count =3D 0; scene_add_obj=
ect(&amp;sc,&amp;keep_obj);</code> is safe, as long as no dynamic alloc. Bu=
t the layers/groups arrays in the scene remain. The keep_obj references a l=
ayer name that exists in sc.layers. Good.</p>
<p>Actually even simpler and safest: I don't need to isolate to a single ob=
ject. The requirement of section 6 is "each object type round-trips". I can=
 verify per object type by: for each real object, scene_write the WHOLE fix=
ture scene and reparse (already done in section 1 for all fixtures). But th=
at doesn't isolate per-type for a clean assertion.</p>
<p>Actually, the cleanest correctness check: For each object type t, find a=
 real object of that type, copy it into a fresh minimal scene where I ALSO =
copy the source scene's layer/group definitions. Let me just do the "keep o=
ne object" approach with obj_count reset.</p>
