9em;"><p>The JSON is on stdout but there are other lines printed to stdout =
mixed in (the "PARSE_OK validate=3DPBT_OK" and "frame written" lines go to =
stdout, not stderr!). That breaks the JSON. The summary is printed to stdou=
t but other printf debug lines also go to stdout. I need the JSON summary t=
o be the ONLY stdout, or capture only the last line.</p>
<p>Actually, those "PARSE_OK" and "frame written" lines =E2=80=94 where do =
they come from? They're from simcheck/scenecheck/framegen being spawned? No=
, those go to their own stdout (the child process), and since tests.exe is =
the parent, the child's stdout is inherited and appears in the parent's std=
out. So when I run <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">./build/tests.exe</code>,=
 the spawned tools' stdout interleaves. The final JSON is the last line, bu=
t there's extra data before it.</p>
<p>For the JSON summary to be clean, I should send the summary to stdout bu=
t ensure spawned tools don't pollute. The spawned tools print to the inheri=
ted stdout. To keep tests.exe's own summary clean, I could print the summar=
y to stderr, or close/redirect. But the spec says "machine-readable summary=
" =E2=80=94 typically stdout.</p>
<p>Simplest fix: make the summary the only thing on stdout by having the sp=
awned tool calls redirect their stdout. But _spawnl inherits the parent's s=
tdout. I could pass the child's stdout to nul... but the tools write to std=
out and we don't capture it. Actually for the test we only check return cod=
e. So I can redirect the child's stdout to NUL via the command. On Windows,=
 <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">_spawnl</code> doesn't take a redirection.<=
/p>
<p>Alternative: print the JSON summary to stderr instead of stdout, and hav=
e the harness read stderr. But convention is stdout.</p>
<p>Better: For the determinism JSON capture, I'll just take the LAST line o=
f output. In my Python I'll read all of stdout and parse the last JSON obje=
ct (the summary line). Let me adjust: capture full stdout, take the line st=
arting with <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">{"tests"</code>.</p>
<p>Actually the spawned tools print their own <code class=3D"cr-inline-code=
">{"ok":true,...}</code> JSON (simcheck) and <code class=3D"cr-inline-code"=
>frame written</code> and <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">PARSE_OK</code>. T=
he tests.exe summary is the LAST line (printf at end). So I can grab the la=
st line. Let me just parse the last non-empty line.</p>
<p>Let me re-run and capture last line. Also note object_types category sho=
ws 0 =E2=80=94 wait, that's wrong. Section 6 (object_types) should have 45 =
checks. But it shows 0. Why? Because the assignment <code class=3D"cr-inlin=
e-code">g_cur_cat=3DCAT_OBJT;</code> was inserted at line 407, but maybe th=
