<li>Free function.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>yaml.c</strong> =E2=80=94 minimal YAML subset parser producing a=
 similar value tree (mappings, block lists, scalars string/int/bool, commen=
ts). This is more complex. I'll implement a line-based parser:</p>
<ul>
<li>Strip <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">#</code> comments (outside quotes)=
.</li>
<li>Detect indentation.</li>
<li>Mappings: <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">key: value</code> or <code cla=
ss=3D"cr-inline-code">key:</code> followed by nested (indented) block.</li>
<li>Block sequences: <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">- item</code> (item can=
 be scalar or mapping).</li>
<li>Scalars: unquoted =E2=86=92 try int, bool, else string. Quoted strings.=
</li>
<li>Produce JsonValue tree (same structure) so locscan can consume uniforml=
y.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>locscan.c</strong> =E2=80=94 reads config (JSON or YAML), then w=
alks the project directory (from argv or config root), counting lines per f=
ile, categorizing by category_rules, excluding by exclude_extensions/exclud=
e_paths/include_extensions, max_file_bytes, binary detection (NUL bytes). O=
utputs human table + JSON (with --json).</p>
<p><strong>releasecheck.c</strong> =E2=80=94 reads RELEASE_RESULT.json and =
RELEASE_EVIDENCE.json paths (or defaults), validates:</p>
<ul>
<li>RELEASE_RESULT schema (required keys, gate statuses enum, tests.total&g=
t;=3D420, determinism.all_match bool, etc.)</li>
<li>RELEASE_EVIDENCE: 163 requirement entries, each with required fields, s=
tatus enum, at least one evidence ref for PASS, verification_methods enum, =
