<li>Block sequences: <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">- scalar</code> or <cod=
e class=3D"cr-inline-code">- key: value</code> (mapping items).</li>
<li>Scalars: unquoted =E2=86=92 detect int/bool/null/string; quoted strings=
 <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">"..."</code> or <code class=3D"cr-inline-co=
de">'...'</code>.</li>
<li>Indentation-based nesting (spaces).</li>
</ul>
<p>This is moderately complex but doable. Let me implement a parser that:</=
p>
<ol>
<li>Split into lines, strip trailing CR.</li>
<li>Skip blank/comment lines.</li>
<li>Tokenize each line into (indent, content).</li>
<li>Recursive parse: parse_block(lines, index, indent) returns a JValue (ob=
ject or array) based on first line.</li>
</ol>
<p>Algorithm:</p>
<ul>
<li>parse_node(lines, *idx, indent):
<ul>
<li>Look at current line at *idx. Determine its indent <code class=3D"cr-in=
line-code">ind</code> and whether it's a sequence item (<code class=3D"cr-i=
nline-code">- </code> prefix) or mapping key (<code class=3D"cr-inline-code=
">key:</code>).</li>
<li>If sequence item: it's an array. Parse all consecutive lines with inden=
t =3D=3D ind that start with <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">- </code>. For =
each, content after <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">- </code> is either:
<ul>
<li>a scalar =E2=86=92 J_STR/int/bool value.</li>
<li><code class=3D"cr-inline-code">key: value</code> =E2=86=92 mapping (par=
se_mapping_inline) OR a nested block (if next lines are indented more) =E2=
=86=92 recurse.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Else mapping: parse all consecutive lines with indent =3D=3D ind that a=
re <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">key: ...</code>. For each:
<ul>
<li>if <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">key: value</code> on same line =E2=86=
=92 store value (scalar or nested if value is <code class=3D"cr-inline-code=
">[</code>/<code class=3D"cr-inline-code">{</code>? we don't support flow, =
skip).</li>
<li>if <code class=3D"cr-inline-code">key:</code> (no value) =E2=86=92 next=
 lines indented more =E2=86=92 recurse parse_node for that child key.</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p>Let me implement carefully. I'll write yaml.c.</p>
